@startuml gonzo_docker_plugin
hide footbox

title Docker Plugin - Detailed Flow

actor User
participant "Docker Plugin" as docker
database "Docker\nDaemon" as daemon
participant "Adapter" as adapter
participant "Gonzo\nPipeline" as gonzo

== Configuration ==
User -> docker: --source='docker:{"follow":["nginx","apache"]}'
docker -> docker: Parse config:\n- endpoint: unix:///var/run/docker.sock\n- followFilters: ["nginx", "apache"]\n- interval: 10s

== Startup ==
docker -> daemon: Connect via Docker API
daemon --> docker: Connection established
docker -> docker: Get hostname & version
docker -> docker: Start containerDiscoveryLoop()

== Container Discovery Loop ==
loop Every 10 seconds
    docker -> daemon: ContainerList(running only)
    daemon --> docker: List of containers
    
    alt New container matching filter
        docker -> docker: Start tailContainerLogs(container)
        create "Log Tailer" as tailer
        docker -> tailer: Start goroutine
        tailer -> daemon: ContainerLogs(follow=true)
    end
end

== Log Processing ==
tailer -> daemon: Read log stream
daemon --> tailer: Log lines with Docker metadata
tailer -> tailer: Parse Docker log format\n(remove timestamps, prefixes)
tailer -> docker: createLogEntry(container, line)
docker -> docker: Create LogEntry with:\n- Source.Type = "docker"\n- Source.Identifier = container_name\n- Attributes: container.id, container.name, etc.
docker -> adapter: LogEntry via channel

== Adapter Conversion ==
adapter -> adapter: convertToJSON(LogEntry)
note right
{
  "timestamp": 1234567890,
  "message": "nginx log line",
  "severity": "INFO",
  "_source": {
    "type": "docker",
    "identifier": "nginx"
  },
  "attributes": {
    "container.name": "nginx",
    "container.id": "abc123..."
  }
}
end note
adapter -> gonzo: JSON string

== Gonzo Processing ==
gonzo -> gonzo: extractSourceInfo(json)
note right: Finds _source.type="docker"\nMaps to "D"\nAssigns ID=1 for first nginx
gonzo -> gonzo: Create tui.LogEntry:\n- SourceType = "D"\n- SourceID = 1
gonzo -> User: Display "D1" in log view

@enduml
